Make codeml's branch-length convergence tolerance settable at runtime.

Forestry declares `e = 1e-8` (codeml.c:612) and passes it unchanged to minB as
e0 (codeml.c:756). minB's only convergence exit is

    if ((dl = fabs(*lnL - lnL0)) < e0 && e <= 0.02) break;

where dl is a whole round's lnL improvement. On a large tree that test cannot
fire. Measured on OG0000000 of the fish run (690 seqs, 12454 codons, 1377
branches): round improvements reach 8.5e-4 by round 11 and the per-round
epsilon then pins at minB's hardcoded 1e-6 floor, so rounds settle at ~1e-6 of
improvement each. Reaching 1e-8 from there needs 450-2300 further rounds
against a hard cap of maxr = 200, and minB's own "too slow" bail-out is gated
on ntime0 < 200 so it never fires either.

The fit therefore always runs exactly 200 rounds. Its stopping point is a round
count, not a converged optimum -- which is worth knowing before treating the
full-length fit as a gold standard it is not.

This patch lets PAML_MINB_E0 override e0 for the com.method == 1 path only.
Unset, the binary is bit-identical to stock. Nothing else reads e before the
call, so the override is complete.

The message is deliberately not gated on `noisy`: ks.py runs codeml with
noisy = 0, and _run_paml captures the console into the PamlRun, so printing it
unconditionally is what makes an override visible in the run's own record. A
result whose provenance you cannot check afterwards is not worth the time saved.

Values, from the OG0000000 round trace:

    PAML_MINB_E0=0.01     stops after round 8    (dl 4.896e-3 -> 1.100e-3)
    PAML_MINB_E0=0.0015   stops after round 10   (dl 1.100e-3 -> 8.540e-4)
    unset                 200 rounds

REBUILD
-------
Keep the existing binary. The comparison needs both, and it is the only way
back if the patched one misbehaves.

1. Apply. The hunk above is documentation, not a machine-applicable diff --
   `patch` will reject it. Use this instead; it is idempotent and refuses to
   guess if the source has moved on:

   cd "${PAML_SRC}"
   cp -n src/codeml.c src/codeml.c.orig
   python3 - src/codeml.c <<'EOF'
import io, sys
p = sys.argv[1]; s = io.open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
if "PAML_MINB_E0" in s:
    sys.exit("already patched")
old = ("            if (com.method == 1)\n"
       "               j = minB(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, x, xb, e, com.space);\n")
if s.count(old) != 1:
    sys.exit("call site not found or not unique -- apply by hand")
new = ("            if (com.method == 1) {\n"
       "               /* divergence: e is the literal 1e-8 from Forestry's\n"
       "                  declaration and is unreachable on large trees. */\n"
       "               const char *e0env = getenv(\"PAML_MINB_E0\");\n"
       "               double e0 = (e0env && *e0env) ? atof(e0env) : e;\n"
       "               if (e0 != e)\n"
       "                  printf(\"\\nminB e0 overridden: %g (default %g)\\n\", e0, e);\n"
       "               j = minB(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, x, xb, e0, com.space);\n"
       "            }\n")
io.open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(s.replace(old, new))
print("patched")
EOF

   The python body is flush left on purpose -- a heredoc keeps leading spaces
   and an indented block is an IndentationError.

2. Compile with the SAME flags as the existing binary, or the comparison
   measures the compiler rather than the tolerance. If they are not written
   down, `history | grep -i znver4` or the build script you used; failing that,
   `readelf -p .comment "${WS}/bin/codeml"` at least pins the compiler version.

       cd src
       cc -O3 -march=znver4 -funroll-loops -o codeml-e0 codeml.c tools.c -lm
       install -m 755 codeml-e0 "${WS}/bin/codeml-e0"

   znver4 needs a Zen 4 host to build on as well as to run on, so do this in a
   job on the amd9654 constraint, not on the login node.

3. Verify the unpatched path is unchanged, on a small orthogroup, before
   trusting anything:

       PAML_MINB_E0= recovery/2_run_orthogroup.sh ...   # with codeml-e0
       # the resulting mlc and *_ks.tsv must match the old binary's exactly.

   If they differ with the variable unset, the rebuild changed something other
   than this patch -- stop and find out what.

4. Then compare tolerances:

       recovery/6_compare_fits.sh <strict>_ks.tsv <loose>_ks.tsv

--- a/src/codeml.c
+++ b/src/codeml.c
@@
          if (iteration && np) {
-            if (com.method == 1)
-               j = minB(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, x, xb, e, com.space);
+            if (com.method == 1) {
+               /* divergence: e is the literal 1e-8 from Forestry's declaration
+                  and is unreachable on large trees; allow it to be set. */
+               const char *e0env = getenv("PAML_MINB_E0");
+               double e0 = (e0env && *e0env) ? atof(e0env) : e;
+               if (e0 != e) printf("\nminB e0 overridden: %g (default %g)\n", e0, e);
+               j = minB(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, x, xb, e0, com.space);
+            }
             else if (com.method == 3)
                j = minB2(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, x, xb, e, com.space);
             else
                j = ming2(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, com.plfun, NULL, x, xb, com.space, e, np);
